MobileGlues: BC formats checked by drawing them, and every step that can crash logged first.

A Pixel 10's PowerVR lists no S3TC in OpenGL ES, while its Vulkan driver samples BC, and the ASTC encoder that
stood in for it crashed the driver's compiler on Android 16 (Pocket Foundry #65). Now each S3TC kind the driver
doesn't list counts as native when a block of it, made as the game makes its atlases, draws as the CPU decodes it
(BC1 there, not BC2), and listed RGTC counts only when it does too. The driver's name, version and extensions are
logged, as is each check, and the encoder's compile and link before the driver takes them.

